NXR-142|Annotated sources and minimal application build|Documentation|The project shall publish commented C++ contracts, a complete current-port assembly explanation and a reproducible minimal application build in its Sphinx manual.|Keep implementation ownership and machine-state assumptions reviewable without a separate undocumented startup boundary.|Sphinx includes actual source listings; every startup/context instruction has a meaningful comment; frame offsets match the constructor; the nano walkthrough identifies clock and map inputs, commands, ELF/map outputs and memory inspection; native and firmware checks pass without claiming board execution.|Strict Sphinx build, source/frame review, cross-build and comparison of emitted assembly text; target register preservation remains a separate gate.|NXR-007,NXR-141|Existing nano profile and documentation build; no new runtime service.|Comments and host-side manual add no firmware objects; example retains one static application stack and control block.|include/rtos.hpp,ports/riscue/start.S,ports/riscue/context.S,ports/riscue/rtos_port.hpp,examples/nano.cpp,docs/assembly-port.rst,docs/source-reference.rst,docs/minimal-application.rst|Source comments, live Sphinx listings and a complete nano walkthrough are present; documentation and cross-build checks do not establish physical timer, register or stack correctness.|include/rtos.hpp,ports/riscue/start.S,ports/riscue/context.S,ports/riscue/rtos_port.hpp,examples/nano.cpp,docs/assembly-port.rst,docs/source-reference.rst,docs/minimal-application.rst|CMakeLists.txt,cmake/firmware.cmake|PartialSourceUnverified
